  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14094884/assets/1f75fd33a40639297f38e03b238ec17bc19e6bd4dd81b82dc22eede3a11e2ac4.png)\n\nConsider the vector $v$ shown above. Find the vector $Av$ given that \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "Notice that $A$ is a rotation-scaling matrix. So, we need to find its scale factor and the angle of rotation.\n\nWe can find the scale factor using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\sqrt{det(A)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(0)^{2}+{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{0+\\frac{1}{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent $A$ as a product of a rotation and a scaling matrix, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}r & 0 \\\\ 0 & r\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta  & -\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta  \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta  & \\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta \\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain that\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta =-1\\end{aligned}\\,\u27f9\\,\\theta =-\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, in order to find $Av$, we need to rotate $v$ clockwise by an angle of $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and scale the result by a scale factor of $\\frac{1}{2},$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14094884/assets/429a6a87ef44d77d0bd199a54783f186ccf8dbea2dfc8f82ca3a9f6862ed8820.png)",
